                <pb facs="0310" n="302" sameAs="frus:frus1941v03/pg302"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.20 Defense (M)/1888: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Egypt</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Kirk</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Cairo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-05-01T17:00:00+03:00">May 1, 1941—5 p.m.</date><lb/>[Received
                        May 2—8:20 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>379. Personal for Feis. In continuation of my 347, April 27, 9 a.m. If you are
                    interested in making the operation of vessels pay, it looks as if we might
                    supply a couple of cargoes of American citizens from this part of the world if
                    ships would carry passengers and if we had advance notice of return
                    sailings.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kirk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
